---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import site from '../data/site.json';
---
<Base title="About ReadyGearHub: How We Pick Preparedness Gear" description="ReadyGearHub is a directory of practical preparedness and multi-purpose gear. Here's how we choose listings, how trending ranks work, and how we stay independent.">
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="wrap"><h1>About ReadyGearHub</h1><p class="lead">{site.tagline}</p></div></section>
  <section class="wrap section prose">
    <p>ReadyGearHub is a directory of practical gear for the moments that matter: winter storms, power outages, roadside breakdowns, hurricane season, and everyday life on the homestead. We sort everything into simple <strong>lanes</strong> so you can find what you need fast.</p>
    <h2>How we choose listings</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Established brands with official product pages.</strong> Every listing links to the manufacturer's own page so you can check current specs, safety instructions, and price.</li>
      <li><strong>Multi-purpose first.</strong> We favor gear you'll use all year, not just once in an emergency.</li>
      <li><strong>No made-up numbers.</strong> We don't publish retailer prices, star ratings, or "reviews" we didn't do for gear listings. Retail prices change daily, so we send you to the source. Prices for our own printable guides are listed in the <a href="/shop/">shop</a>.</li>
      <li><strong>Safety matters.</strong> For heaters, generators, and fuel-burning gear, we point to the manufacturer's instructions and carbon monoxide safety.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>What "Trending" means</h2>
    <p>Our listings are maintained with the help of automated tools that watch seasonal demand, weather, and outage news. When a winter storm is in the forecast, for example, radios, heaters, and power stations move up. Trending is a measure of timeliness, not a paid placement. Paid placements, if we offer them, will always be clearly labeled "Featured."</p>
    <h2>How we make money</h2>
    <p>Some links may be affiliate links, which means we may earn a commission if you buy, at no extra cost to you. See our <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">Affiliate Disclosure</a>. We also sell our own printable guides and planners as instant PDF downloads through Payhip, listed in the <a href="/shop/">shop</a>.</p>
    <h2>Get in touch</h2>
    <p>Questions, corrections, or a product we should look at? <a href="/contact/">Contact us</a>.</p>
  </section>
</Base>
